    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3bdea81b_4d79d83b",
        "filename": "chacha20/chacha_generic.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 264,
      "author": {
        "id": 11715
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-17T17:04:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is neat, but it mixes BCE hints and logic. By reading the rest of the code one can tell it\u0027s equivalent, but only looking at this we\u0027d wonder \"why check both dst and src? what if they are 1-63 bytes?\n\nWould it be noticeably slower to do this?\n\n    for len(src) \u003e 0 {\n        _, _ \u003d src[:blockSize], dst[:blockSize] // bounds check elimination hint",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 264,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 264,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "ee0e8efa5ab6ac3b20a446c0ed6947ee3cd5955f",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5867c262_02850d7c",
        "filename": "chacha20/chacha_generic.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 264,
      "author": {
        "id": 35525
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-17T19:48:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think src or dst can be 1-63 bytes, because at the top there is a check on len(dst) \u003d\u003d len(src) and len(dst)%blockSize\u003d\u003d0. Since we are reslicing them by 64 bytes after each loop, src and dst are either a multiple of 64 bytes long or empty (i.e. we are done).\n\nDoing\n    for len(src) \u003e 0 {\n        _, _ \u003d src[:blockSize], dst[:blockSize] // bounds check elimination hint\n\nis surprisingly very expensive\n benchmark                        old ns/op     new ns/op     delta\n BenchmarkChaCha20/64-12          129           141           +9.30%\n BenchmarkChaCha20/256-12         433           480           +10.85%\n BenchmarkChaCha20/10x25-12       769           814           +5.85%\n BenchmarkChaCha20/4096-12        433           479           +10.62%\n BenchmarkChaCha20/100x40-12      7911          8652          +9.37%\n BenchmarkChaCha20/65536-12       103723        115899        +11.74%\n BenchmarkChaCha20/1000x65-12     106253        117951        +11.01%\n\n benchmark                        old MB/s     new MB/s     speedup\n BenchmarkChaCha20/64-12          494.42       452.39       0.91x\n BenchmarkChaCha20/256-12         590.71       533.55       0.90x\n BenchmarkChaCha20/10x25-12       325.11       307.00       0.94x\n BenchmarkChaCha20/4096-12        591.66       534.14       0.90x\n BenchmarkChaCha20/100x40-12      505.65       462.34       0.91x\n BenchmarkChaCha20/65536-12       631.83       565.46       0.89x\n BenchmarkChaCha20/1000x65-12     611.75       551.08       0.90x\n\nThis also doesn\u0027t eliminate the BCE at the end of the loop\n src, dst \u003d src[blockSize:], dst[blockSize:]\n\nDoing\n _, _ \u003d src[blockSize-1], dst[blockSize-1]\n\ninstead eliminates the BCE on the reslicing at the end of the loop, but it still slows down the benchmark by 1.6-4.8%",
      "parentUuid": "3bdea81b_4d79d83b",
